<title>UK: SevernTrent buys back 2.5 mln shares at 661p.</title>
<headline>SevernTrent buys back 2.5 mln shares at 661p.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British water and sewerage company Severn Trent said on Tuesday it had bought back 2.5 million of its own shares at 661 pence each from brokers ABN AMRO Hoare Govett.</p>
<p>The government earlier sold off its remaining stakes in a group of privatised utilities to raise 257 million pounds.  </p>
<p>Severn Trent said ABN AMRO Hoare Govett had approached the company after the broker bought about 3.57 million Severn Trent shares from the government.</p>
<p>The share buy-back represents less than one percent of Severn Trent's share capital.</p>
<p>The government also sold off its remaining holdings in National Grid, Northern Ireland Electricity, Scottish Hydro-Electric, National Power, PowerGen, South West Water and Wessex Water and most of its stake in nuclear generator British Energy.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
